&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    Although #2750 enable the support of spark 2.3, it breaks the support of spark 1.6. Users have to build zeppelin against spark 1.6 to make zeppelin work with that. But previous one zeppelin instance can work with multiple versions of spark. This PR introduce spark shims module which is to resolve the api incompatible issue between different versions of spark, so that one zeppelin instance can work with multiple versions of spark. &lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
